2 CONC B 10.68.41: The Lord angrily dug up Hastinapura with the tip of His plow and began to drag it, intending to cast the entire city into the Ganges. SB 10.68.42-43: Seeing that their city was tumbling about like a raft at sea as it w
2 CONC as being dragged away, and that it was about to fall into the Ganges, the Kauravas became terrified. To save their lives they approached the Lord for shelter, taking their families with them. Placing Samba and Lakshmana in front, 
