1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Draupadi''' (Sanskrit: द्रौपदी, IAST: draupadī, lit. Daughter of Drupada), also referred as Panchalī, is the Heroine in the Hindu epic, Mahabharata. She was the daughter of King Drupada of Panchal, most beautifu
2 CONC l woman of her time and common wife of the Pandavas who fought their cousins, the Kauravas in the great Kurukshetra War. She had five sons, who were collectively addressed as the Upapandavas[1] and six daughters. Hence, she had tw
2 CONC o children from each Pandava.
